Let `GDAL_LIBS` override the list of libraries pyogrio's extensions link
against, so the iOS slices can name GDAL's whole static dependency chain.

Unlike fiona and rasterio, pyogrio already supports an environment-driven
build: `get_gdal_config()` uses `GDAL_INCLUDE_PATH`, `GDAL_LIBRARY_PATH` and
`GDAL_VERSION` when all three are set, and only falls back to shelling out
to `gdal-config` when they are not. (Note the spelling — `GDAL_LIBRARY_PATH`
here, `GDAL_LIB_PATH` in fiona/rasterio; each recipe's `script_env` matches
its own package. Each is a single directory, not a list.) That covers the
headers, the library search path and the version, which is why this recipe
needs no path patching at all.

What it does not cover is *which* libraries to link: `gdal_libs` is hard-
wired to `["gdal"]`, with one Windows-only special case for the older
`gdal_i` import library. On Android that is correct — libgdal is a shared
object and the dynamic linker pulls its dependencies in behind it — so
`meta.yaml` leaves `GDAL_LIBS` unset there and the upstream default stands.
On iOS every native dep is built `-DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF`, and when
`libgdal.a` was archived the linker kept only the objects GDAL itself
referenced; symbols like `_geod_init` (libproj), `_TIFFClientOpen` (libtiff)
and `_psl_builtin` (libpsl) were left undefined in it. `_io`/`_ogr` inherit
those undefined references, `-undefined dynamic_lookup` defers them to
dlopen, and iOS dyld — which resolves the flat namespace eagerly — aborts on
the first miss at `import pyogrio`. Setting
`GDAL_LIBS=gdal,proj,tiff,curl,psl,sqlite3,jpeg,ssl,crypto,z` makes
pyogrio's own link command pull those objects straight out of the
archives. The comma is the separator because these are library names, not
paths; `meta.yaml` carries the full rationale and the pointer to the proper
long-term fix in `flet-libgdal`'s iOS cmake invocation.

Without this patch the Android wheel is unaffected but the iOS wheel builds
green and then fails to load on device.

Rationale is recorded: the patch was added in PR #65 ("Support testing
recipes on Android emulator and iOS simulator and fixes issues found"),
whose description names this dyld flat-namespace cascade as one of the
failures the new on-device tests surfaced across gdal / pyogrio / rasterio.

diff --git a/setup.py b/setup.py
--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -59,6 +59,8 @@

     if include_dir and library_dir and gdal_version_str:
         gdal_libs = ["gdal"]
+        if "GDAL_LIBS" in os.environ:
+            gdal_libs = os.environ["GDAL_LIBS"].split(",")

         if platform.system() == "Windows":
             # NOTE: if libgdal is built for Windows using CMake, it is now "gdal",
